# Calibration table — estimate vs actual

**This file is project-owned.** It ships as a seed prior and is meant to be
overwritten by your own measurements; `copier update` will not touch it once it
exists. `SKILL.md` holds the method, this file holds the numbers.

Actual = focused time to done (journal sessions; fallback ticket-create →
PR-created, both UTC), review-wait excluded. Ratio = estimate / actual.

## Unit anchors

Every range should be the measured spread of the actuals behind it, so a shape
with one data point is marked — treat those as provisional, not as precision.

Until this project has rows of its own, the ranges below are a **prior** carried
over from the Odoo project this skill came from (Claude-assisted delivery, small
custom-module changes on a live ERP). They are a starting bet, not a
measurement of *your* work: replace each one with your own spread, and its
`Behind it` cell with your own ticket keys, as the table below fills up.

| Shape | Focused hours | Behind it |
|---|---|---|
| View-only change (hide/show/reorder fields, labels) | 0.3–0.5 | prior |
| Fix, root cause already known (traceback / user points at it) | 0.3–0.5 | prior |
| Fix needing diagnosis (reproduce, locate the seam) | 0.5–1 | prior |
| Small feature: field/button + tests, one module | 0.5–1 | prior |
| Retire a model/feature incl. dependent cleanup + migration | 1–1.5 | prior |
| Mechanical repo-wide sweep (lint, warnings, renames) | 1–2 | prior |
| Audit a repo-wide problem, decide how to stage it, ship one half | 2–3 | prior |
| Prod data repair + live verification | 3–4 | prior |
| Multi-item batch through the full gate (QC, docs, PR, deploy) | 5–6 | prior |

Fixed adder to measure for yourself and record here: the constant tail of every
delivery — deploy, announcement, post-deploy invariant check.

